<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Protected</h1>
<p>Every new character is a <b>protected</b> citizen: the law looks after you. 
If someone steals from you or kills you, it is a crime, and the law goes 
after them. Most townsfolk are protected too: guards, shopkeepers, mayors and so on.
</p><p>You lose your protection when you break the law and get caught: a few crimes 
and the law no longer looks after you; more, and the guards are after you 
(see <a cmd='#'>Help Crimes</a>). After you have served your time in jail, you are 
protected again.
</p><p><b>Deputies.</b> A protected citizen with a clean record can become a deputy: 
go to the Captain in Midgaard and type <a cmd='#'>join</a>. Deputies can arrest wanted 
criminals and take them to jail, and the police academy teaches them things 
nobody else can learn, such as hand cuffing (see <a cmd='#'>Help Cuff</a>). You stay in your 
own guild too. But if you are ever accused of a crime, the Captain throws you 
out for good, and you lose what the academy taught you.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
